 "note": "Defender AG spread ON by default (2026-09-24). GOB_DEFENDER_AG_SPREAD widens the PLAYER multiplier for DEFENDERS ONLY to (1 - s) + (AG/100) * 2s at s = DEFENDER_AG_SPREAD = 0.50, keeping AG=50 fixed so the average player never moves and the flag cannot be a stealth global speed change. The spread is applied PER PLAYER by def_lineup membership (animation_step_helpers.defender_aware_rate) -- never by an action label -- so the OFFENCE is untouched at every archetype and AG. It reaches the endpoint AND the duration through the single accessor shared.movement_rate built in Stage 1, which is why the render/sim divergence at this default is 0.0221% (147 of 666,385 placements) against a 0.0301% floor with the flag off; it was 7.95% before the unification. ROLLBACK IS SYMMETRIC AND EXACT: GOB_DEFENDER_AG_SPREAD=0 reproduces equiv_v3_reference_1f4af0ede_loosesag_nogate.json 160/160 on fingerprint AND draws in all four cells, and equiv_v3_loose_baseline_1f4af0ede_loosesag.json 80/80 -- verified at the flip, not assumed. Nothing retuned; s was already 0.50 in the code. What a player sees: the p10-AG vs p90-AG arrival gap is 1.90 grid units mean (was 0.35), above the ~0.5-unit visibility floor on 40.6% of moving placements, but the median is still 0.000, so most placements look unchanged. The loose footing has its own baseline, equiv_v3_loose_baseline_f600628a4_agspread.json. See reports/ag-spread-default-flip.md.",
